🧩 PATTERN (very important):
Frequency / Seen-Before Pattern

This pattern is:
used with HashMap / HashSet
used in substring, array, sliding window problems
the bridge between collections knowledge and DSA logic

In one line, when would you use HashSet instead of HashMap?
“HashSet is used when we only need to store unique elements and perform fast existence checks, without associating any value with the elements.”

🧠 Why this answer is correct
Unique elements → HashSet
Fast lookup (contains) → O(1)
No key–value mapping needed → HashMap not required
You now clearly know when to choose HashSet vs HashMap.

If you want to check whether an element has appeared before (yes/no), would you use HashSet or HashMap? Why?
“I would use HashSet because I only need to check presence (yes/no) using contains(),
whereas HashMap is needed only when I must store additional information like counts or values.”

🧠 Why this distinction matters (lock this in)
Think in questions, not in code:
Ask yourself:
“Do I need only existence, or do I need information?”

Need	                    Use
Seen before?(yes/no)	    HashSet
How many times?	            HashMap
Last index / first index	HashMap
Any value mapping	        HashMap

🔑 One mental rule (very important)
If the answer is boolean → HashSet
If the answer is a number or value → HashMap

